      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, im stuck on a literature review. if a paper has 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th vs Chicago style? i want to make sure i dont mess up the format for the dissertation.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In APA 7th edition, for a paper with 5 authors, the in-text citation would be Smith et al. (2020). In this format, the et al. abbreviates the authors' names at the end of the citation.\n\nIn Chicago style, the in-text citation for a 5-author paper would be (Smith et al., 2020). However, according to the Chicago style, if there are 7 or more authors, you would use the fewer number first, so (Smith, W. et al., 2020).",
