      "content": "In APA 7th edition, you don't need to use \"et al.\" on the first mention of a study with 2-10 authors. Instead, you would list every author's name. However, with 11 or more authors, \"et al.\" is indeed used. For a study with 5 authors, you would list the first author's name and then list the remaining authors after the first author's name, separated by commas.",
